From ee0b3b6ae938cf17ee8440ed5778fc9386d0b6a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:50:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ingress: refuse a declared authority effect other than
 NONE before the crossing

StegVerse-Labs/.github#3369 ("missing authority"). The crossing copies
manifest.transition.authority_effect onto the InTr envelope verbatim and
process_boundary.py passes it through to its result, while the boundary
document resolves effects as DERIVED_FROM_APPLICABLE_TRANSITION_ELEMENTS and
both ledger appends record "NONE". Nothing on the receive() path checked it.

receive() now refuses any declared effect that is not NONE -- an absent
transition or authority_effect is NONE, read exactly as the crossing reads
it -- before cross() is called, so the endpoint never runs under it. The
refusal is recorded at both ledger levels through _refused, with the six
fields: AUTHORITY_EFFECT_NOT_WARRANTED_AT_INGRESS /
DECLARED_AUTHORITY_EFFECT_IS_NONE_UNTIL_A_WARRANT_RECEIPT_BINDS, owned by
SDK-MANIFEST-ECOSYSTEM-TRANSITION-DISPOSITION-001. Every manifest the
ingress, crossing and role-conformance tests send, and the pinned SDK's
builders, declare NONE or nothing.

The conformance fixture n6 (MISSING_AUTHORITY) now exercises this refusal
(n6-authority-effect-not-warranted, COVERED_WITH_SPEC_GAP); its remaining gap
is a warranted effect, which waits on a landed TV/TVC warrant receipt
(AUTHORITY_WARRANT_RECEIPT_NOT_VERIFIED_AT_INGRESS). The absent-resolution
refusal n6 covered before is kept as an ordering test in the new
tests/test_organization_ingress_authority_effect.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
